@{
    Layout = "_PageShell";
    ViewData["Heading"] = "Privacy policy";
    var meta = ViewData.Meta();
    meta.Title = "Privacy policy";
    meta.Description = "What information The Meridian Newsfolio collects, how it is used and the choices you have.";
    meta.Breadcrumbs.Add(("Privacy policy", SeoUrls.Page("/privacy")));
}

<p class="lead">This policy explains what information The Meridian Newsfolio collects and how we use it.</p>

<h2>Information we collect</h2>
<p>When you create an account we store your name, email address and a hashed version of your password. We never store the password itself. When you comment, we store the comment text and the time it was posted. We count article views from signed-in readers to show trending stories.</p>
<p>When you are signed in, we keep a list of the stories you open (your reading history) so we can recommend similar stories. If you are not signed in, the last few stories you opened are remembered only for your current visit.</p>

<h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
<p>We use a session cookie to keep you signed in, a security cookie that protects forms against cross-site request forgery, and a cookie that remembers your language. Your light or dark theme choice is stored in your browser. We do not use advertising cookies.</p>

<h2>How we use information</h2>
<p>Account information is used to sign you in, show your name next to your comments and contact you about your account. We do not sell personal information.</p>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>You can update your name and password from your profile. You can see, remove or clear your reading history at any time on the <a href="/history">Reading history</a> page. To have your account removed, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>We will update this page if our practices change.</p>
